    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Spring weather conditions arrived along a stretch of the U.S. border, making crossings more survivable for ordinary people caught by the system. The numbers show a seasonal bump: apprehensions increased from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. Those apprehended at the border are part of the affected population, while elected officials who set the rules everyone else lives under remain deadlocked over funding for the agencies that affect everyone's daily reality.",
