    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The system is holding the line: year-to-date crossings remain near multi-decade lows under asylum shutdown and deportation policies, and ordinary people bear the cost. Observers tracking the data point to a documented rise in border apprehensions between February and March, a border activity metric tied to milder spring weather. Meanwhile, a political stalemate over agency funding leaves the agencies enforcing immigration laws at the border without new money in a pending reconciliation package.",
